-- 10-storage.sql
--
-- Extracted from artifacts/v1/gaos-arcadedb-model.html, which is the source of
-- truth for this schema, THEN RECONCILED against ArcadeDB 26.7.2. This file is
-- not verbatim: see RECONCILIATION.md, deviation 2 -- the one deviation that is
-- a design error in the model rather than a dialect difference.
--
-- Do not edit this file to change the model -- change the document, then
-- re-extract and re-reconcile.
--
-- Applied in filename order by deploy/schema/apply.sh, last, because every
-- statement here ALTERs a type the earlier files created.
--
-- These are ALTER rather than CREATE, so there is no IF NOT EXISTS to carry.
-- They are idempotent for the other reason: setting the same bucket strategy
-- or the same EXTERNAL flag twice is the same assignment twice, not a
-- redeclaration. This file is T-004 (bucket-partition by tenantId, J-3/BR-26)
-- and T-005 (heavy payloads stored EXTERNAL, BR-25) in their entirety.

-- Route records to buckets by tenant so one tenant's write burst does not
-- contend with another's, and so a per-tenant export is a bucket-local scan.
--
-- WITHDRAWN against ArcadeDB 26.7.2 -- see RECONCILIATION.md, deviation 2.
-- This is not a syntax problem. `partitioned(p)` requires a UNIQUE index on
-- exactly (p), and a unique index on tenantId means one Task per tenant. That
-- was measured, not reasoned about: with the index in place, inserting a
-- second Task for tenant 'loop-eng' fails with DuplicatedKeyException. The
-- strategy exists to partition by primary key, which tenantId is not.
--
-- What the three lines below were buying is preserved by other means, and
-- BR-26's actual requirement -- "tenantId declared and indexed whatever the
-- tenancy strategy turns out to be" -- is met by 09-indexes.sql either way:
--   Task    (tenantId, id)               UNIQUE
--   TaskRun (tenantId, id)               UNIQUE
--   Event   (tenantId, seq)              UNIQUE
--   Task    (tenantId, status, priority) NOTUNIQUE
-- and isolation rests where D-042 puts it: database-per-tenant as the default,
-- with tenantId as the second line rather than the first.
--
-- ALTER TYPE Task    BucketSelectionStrategy `partitioned('tenantId')`;
-- ALTER TYPE TaskRun BucketSelectionStrategy `partitioned('tenantId')`;
-- ALTER TYPE Event   BucketSelectionStrategy `partitioned('tenantId')`;

-- Heavy, rarely projected payloads move out of the topology page.
-- Available from v26.5.1; check your version before relying on it.
ALTER PROPERTY ContextSlice.rendered EXTERNAL true;
ALTER PROPERTY Prompt.template       EXTERNAL true;
ALTER PROPERTY Artifact.body         EXTERNAL true;
